Package: thangldKANr
Type: Package
Title: Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks with Interchangeable Edge Bases Using
        'torch'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Thang", family = "Le-Dinh",
           email = "thang87sg@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Implements Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks (KAN) in R on top of the
    'torch' package (no 'Python' needed) with one network engine and
    interchangeable edge bases: Chebyshev, Legendre and Jacobi polynomials,
    Gaussian radial basis functions (FastKAN), Mexican hat wavelets (Bozorgasl
    and Chen (2024) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2405.12832>), safe Pade rational
    functions (Molina, Schramowski and Kersting (2020)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1907.06732>), a hybrid of SiLU, Chebyshev and radial
    basis parts, and squared rectified linear unit bumps (Qiu et al. (2024)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2406.02075>). Each layer may use a different basis,
    and further bases can be registered by other packages. Besides tabular
    regression, the same layers power graph KANs for node regression
    (neighbourhood aggregation with the normalized adjacency matrix, as in
    Kiamari, Kiamari and Krishnamachari (2024)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2406.06470>) and lag-window KANs for one-step time
    series forecasting. Provides multi-layer networks with Adam training,
    training-only standardization, validation-based early stopping,
    reproducible seeds, edge-function evaluation and plots, and model
    persistence. A base R reference implementation with analytic gradients
    serves as a numerical oracle and as a training backend that does not
    need 'libtorch'. The network follows Liu et al. (2024)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2404.19756>.
